    {
      "id": "c30aa255f80e2ff1b5d26f9e7ee765a4161c1459",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1733638556,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> x11 dissector is not a generate dissector ?\n\nSome of it is, some of it isn't; packet-x11.c isn't.  (x11-register-info.h, for example, is.)\n\nI.e., the code to dissect XConfigureWindow requests is *not* generated from the xcb project's xproto.xml file; it's hardcoded, and, apparently, incorrectly so.  Other routines there may also be incorrect.\n\n> (Look README.x11 on epan/dissectors)\n\n(README.X11, capital \"X\" - case matters, unless your copy of the respository is on a case-insensitive file system, which is likely to be the case only on macOS or Windows, and it's not even guaranteed to be the case there.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-01-19T07:20:58.243Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-01-19T09:38:54.191Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 276222560,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 14100,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e856ca86d70e38345b9f81b0023cb56721d0a6a1",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1733640635,
          "type": null,
          "body": "And, yes, if we could generate the dissection code, not just the fields, from the XML files, that would be nice.  .cnf files to make the dissection prettier might be nice, just as we have .cnf file for ASN.1 and DCE RPC generated dissectors.",
